  "result": "All eight tests pass, including the three new namespace tests.\n\nChanges in `kvstore/store.py`:\n\n- **Schema** now has a namespace column. The table is keyed by the pair of namespace and key, so the same key can hold different values in different namespaces within the one file.\n- **Existing methods** set, get, delete, and keys take a keyword argument `ns` defaulting to \"default\" and scope every query to that namespace.\n- **New methods** count returns the number of keys in a namespace, and namespaces returns the sorted distinct namespaces that currently hold at least one key. Both are read straight from the table, so a namespace disappears once its last key is deleted.\n- **Legacy migration** detects a data file written by the previous single-namespace schema and moves its rows into the \"default\" namespace inside one transaction on open. I verified this with a hand-built old-format file.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was changed.",
